      <h3>About Your Due Date</h3>
      <p>Your due date is calculated using Naegele's Rule, which adds 280 days (40 weeks) to the first day of your last menstrual period. This is the standard method used by healthcare providers.</p>
      <p>Remember that only about 5% of babies are born exactly on their due date. Most babies arrive within a week before or after this date.</p>
      
      <div id="trimesterInfo" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <h3>Pregnancy Milestones</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>First Trimester:</strong> Weeks 1-12</li>
          <li><strong>Second Trimester:</strong> Weeks 13-26</li>
          <li><strong>Third Trimester:</strong> Weeks 27-40+</li>
        </ul>
